WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Look at an analog clock, then look away. When you glance back, the first tick may feel strangely long.

2
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
In a 2001 study, researchers tested this impression, called chronostasis.

3
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Their explanation concerns how the brain places an image in time after your eyes move.

4
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
It is not proof that time stopped, or that meditation audio can change your brain.

5
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Our buyer guide separates an interesting perception finding from what a seller actually supplies.

6
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Before paying for a recording, try the free twelve-minute observation and ask what was genuinely tested.
